  "label": "User projected onto the absurd juxtaposition scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the overall absurd juxtaposition scene, where the serious, formal image of Barack Obama is contrasted with the fictional, humorous text 'found bigfoot' and 'married her.' This projection implies the user is imagining themselves or others engaging in the absurd narrative, or at least identifying with the satirical framing of the meme. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you,' but the meme's structure invites the user to mentally inhabit the scenario, projecting their own perspective onto the scene.",
